  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To embed evaluation in the new UK National Action Plan (NAP) on Women, Peace and Security (WPS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To evaluate how we can best implement our UN commitments on Women, Peace and Security. The NAP is designed to ensure that the provisions of UN Security Council Resolution 1325 on Women, Peace and Security (and other associated resolutions) are incorporated into Her Majesty&#x2019;s Government&#x2019;s (HMG&#x2019;s) work on conflict and fragility. The NAP is structured around the four pillars of UNSCR 1325: Participation; Protection; Prevention; and Relief and Recovery. An additional pillar highlights how the UK will build its own capacity for implementation. This includes a commitment to evaluate our progress.</narrative>
  </description>
